      LessonBlock.paragraph("PPSC ke one paper me English ke hisse me article par, yani a, an aur the par, har saal sawal ata hai. Kabhi jumla theek karna hota hai aur kabhi chaar options me se sahi wala chunna hota hai. Aur mazay ki baat suno, ye sawal paper ke sab se asaan number hain. Bas aik chhota sa qanoon samajhna hai. Jo student ye lesson pakka kar le, wo paper me an honest aur a university jaisi ghalti kabhi nahi karega. Aur yaad rakho, yahi wo ghaltiyan hain jin par aadhe se zyada students apne number kaatte hain."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Pehle noun ko samajh lo"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Dekho, sab se pehle noun ko samajh lo, baqi sab khud asaan ho jayega. Tum apne aas paas dekho. Ye kursi, ye meiz, ye kitaab jo tumhare haath me hai, in sab ka koi na koi naam hai. Ali tumhara dost hai, us ka naam Ali hai. Ustad ko ustad kehte hain aur doctor ko doctor. Lahore aik sheher ka naam hai, school aur bazaar jagah ke naam hain. Aur mohabbat? Wo nazar to nahi aati, lekin us ka bhi aik naam hai. Imaandari aur khof bhi naam hi hain, bas ye dil aur dimagh me hote hain."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("English me har naam wali cheez ko noun kehte hain. Bas, baat khatam. Noun ki tareef ratne ki zaroorat nahi. Bas ye tasveer zehen me bitha lo ke jahan naam hai, wahan noun hai. Shakhs ka naam ho, jagah ka naam ho, cheez ka naam ho ya kisi khayal ka naam ho, sab noun hain."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Ab a aur an ki baat"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab a aur an ko samjho. Urdu me hum kehte hain aik kitaab, aik admi. English me yehi \"aik\" kabhi a ban jata hai aur kabhi an. Asal masla sirf itna hai ke kab a lagega aur kab an."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Aik misaal se samjho. Farz karo tum kisi ko chai pila rahe ho. Tum Urdu me kaho ge, aik cup chai. Theek hai. Ab agar cup ki jagah apple aa jaye to? Aik apple. Lekin English me isay an apple kehte hain, a apple nahi. Kyun? Bol kar dekho. Apple bolte hue munh se pehli awaaz \"a\" ki nikalti hai, jo vowel ki awaaz hai. Aur jab pehli awaaz vowel ki ho to zabaan par \"a\" atakta hai aur \"an\" asani se nikalta hai. Angrezon ne apni asani ke liye ye qanoon bana liya."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Qanoon ye hai. Kaan se suno, aankh se mat dekho. Lafz ki pehli awaaz vowel ki ho, yani a, e, i, o, u jaisi awaaz ho, to an lagega. Pehli awaaz consonant ki ho to a lagega."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Yahi is lesson ka asal raaz hai. Letter nahi, awaaz. Kuch alfaaz dekhne me vowel se shuru hote hain lekin awaaz consonant ki dete hain. University ko bol kar dekho, \"yu-niversity\". Aur kuch alfaaz dekhne me consonant se shuru hote hain lekin un ka pehla letter khamosh hota hai. Honest ko bolo to \"onest\" banta hai, h ghayab. Paper hamesha inhi do cheezon par phansata hai, aur is lesson ke baad tum nahi phanso ge."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Aik aur zaroori baat zehen me rakho. A aur an sirf us noun ke sath ata hai jo aik ho aur gina ja sakta ho. Hum Urdu me \"aik pani\" nahi kehte, kyunke pani gina nahi jata. Isi liye English me a water bhi ghalat hai. Aur a books bhi ghalat hai, kyunke books to pehle hi aik se zyada hain."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Board par qanoon Angrezi me"),
      LessonBlock.rule("Ustad jab board par qanoon likhta hai to kuch yun likhta hai. A noun is the name of a person, place, thing or idea. A and an mean \"one\", and they are used only with a singular countable noun. Use an before a word that begins with a vowel sound. Use a before a word that begins with a consonant sound. Aur sab se aham line ye hai: decide by sound, not by spelling. A university, an hour. Aur aakhir me ye bhi yaad rakho ke plural nouns aur uncountable nouns ke sath a ya an kabhi nahi ata."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Misaalein board se"),
