  Lesson(
    id: "grammar-02",
    number: 2,
    title: "Plural Nouns",
    subtitle: "Plural Nouns. Aik se zyada, lekin har noun ka apna andaaz.",
    partIndex: 0,
    partName: "Foundation — Getting Started",
    blocks: <LessonBlock>[
      LessonBlock.heading("Ye lesson kyun zaroori hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("PPSC ke one paper me plural par do tarah ke sawal ate hain. Pehli tarah ke seedhe sawal hote hain, jaise koi pooche ke plural of criterion kya hai. Doosri tarah jumla theek karne wale sawal hote hain, jahan informations, sheeps ya brother-in-laws jaisi ghalti jumle ke andar chhupi hoti hai. Ye sawal un students ke number kaatte hain jo sirf aik usool jante hain ke s laga do, kaam khatam. Sach ye hai ke plural ke chand hi usool hain. Is lesson ke baad tum har noun ka plural khud bana sako ge, rata lagaye baghair."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Plural matlab kya hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Pehle baat samajh lo. Urdu me bhi yehi hota hai. Kitaab aik hai, kitaabein zyada. Larka aik hai, larkay zyada. English me bhi jab noun aik se zyada ho jaye to us ki shakal badal jati hai. Isi badli hui shakal ko plural kehte hain."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Lekin aik baat pehle din se zehen me bitha lo. English me har noun aik hi tareeqe se plural nahi banta. Kuch noun seedha s le lete hain, jaise book se books. Kuch es mangte hain, jaise box se boxes. Kuch apni shakal hi badal dete hain, jaise man se men aur child se children. Aur kuch itne shareef hain ke aik hon ya hazaar, shakal waisi ki waisi rehti hai, jaise sheep se sheep."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Asal raaz: noun ka aakhir dekho"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ghabrane ki koi baat nahi. Ye sab usoolon me bandha hua hai. Tumhe bas ye dekhna hai ke noun khatam kis par ho raha hai. Aakhri letter hi faisla karta hai ke plural kese banega. Jaise darzi kapra dekh kar samajh jata hai ke silai kahan lagegi, waisay hi tum noun ka aakhir dekh kar us ka plural bana lo ge."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Chalo, usool aik aik karke samjhte hain."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Pehla usool sab se aam hai. Sirf s laga do. Book se books, pen se pens, boy se boys. Zyada tar nouns isi usool par chalte hain."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Doosra usool un nouns ke liye hai jo s, x, z, ch ya sh par khatam hon. Un ke aage es lagta hai. Bus se buses, box se boxes, watch se watches, dish se dishes. Kyun? Bol kar dekho. Boxs bolna mushkil hai, boxes zabaan par asaan parta hai. English hamesha asani dekhta hai. Ye baat is lesson me bhi yaad ayegi aur aage bhi."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Teesra usool y walon ka hai. Agar noun consonant ke baad y par khatam ho, jaise city ya baby, to y nikal kar ies lag jata hai. City se cities, baby se babies. Lekin agar y se pehle vowel ho, jaise boy ya day, to sirf s lagta hai. Boy se boys, day se days. Dekha? Y ke peeche wala letter faisla karta hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Chautha usool f aur fe walon ka hai. Kuch nouns jo f ya fe par khatam hon, un ka f ves ban jata hai. Knife se knives, wife se wives, leaf se leaves, half se halves. Lekin khabardar, sab aise nahi hote. Roof se roofs banta hai aur chief se chiefs. Ye seedha s lete hain. Ye chand alfaaz yaad karne wale hain, aur in ki trick aage bata raha hun."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Paanchva usool purane alfaaz ka hai. Ye apni andar ki awaaz badal dete hain. Man se men, woman se women, foot se feet, tooth se teeth, goose se geese, mouse se mice. Aur kuch bilkul khaas hain. Child se children, ox se oxen, person se people. In ka koi shortcut nahi. Ye istemal se yaad hote hain, aur paper inhi ko poochta hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Chhata usool shareef alfaaz ka hai. Sheep, deer, fish, series aur species. Ye aik hon ya zyada, in ki shakal nahi badalti."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Saatva usool mile jule alfaaz ka hai, jinhe compound nouns kehte hain. In me asal lafz plural hota hai, aakhir wala nahi. Brother-in-law ka plural brothers-in-law hai, brother-in-laws nahi. Asal lafz brother hai, law to peeche laga hua hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Aur kuch purane Greek aur Latin alfaaz bhi apna purana tareeqa rakhte hain. Criterion se criteria banta hai aur phenomenon se phenomena. Ye dono paper ke bohat pasandida hain."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Aakhir me aik khaas dhoka samajh lo. Kuch alfaaz dikhne me plural lagte hain lekin hote singular hain. News, mathematics, physics. The news is good hota hai, are nahi. Aur kuch alfaaz hamesha plural rehte hain. Scissors, trousers, glasses. In ka aik wala istemal karna ho to a pair of scissors kehna parta hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Board par qanoon Angrezi me"),
      LessonBlock.rule("Board par ye usool kuch yun likhe jate hain. Most nouns add s, as book becomes books. Nouns ending in s, x, z, ch or sh add es, as box becomes boxes and watch becomes watches. When a noun ends in a consonant plus y, the y changes to ies, as city becomes cities, but after a vowel only s is added, as boy becomes boys. Many nouns ending in f or fe change to ves, as knife becomes knives and leaf becomes leaves, but remember, roof becomes roofs and chief becomes chiefs. Some plurals are irregular: man becomes men, woman becomes women, child becomes children, foot becomes feet, tooth becomes teeth, mouse becomes mice, ox becomes oxen and person becomes people. Some nouns never change: sheep, deer, fish, series and species. In compound nouns the main word becomes plural: brother-in-law becomes brothers-in-law. Aur aakhir me ye line kabhi mat bhulna: news, mathematics and physics look plural but are singular, while scissors, trousers and glasses are always plural."),
