  Lesson(
    id: "grammar-24",
    number: 24,
    title: "Passive Voice ki Buniyad",
    subtitle: "Passive Voice ki Buniyad. Jab kaam aham ho, karne wala nahi",
    partIndex: 7,
    partName: "Voice & Narration",
    blocks: <LessonBlock>[
      LessonBlock.heading("Ye lesson kyun zaroori hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("PPSC ke one paper me passive voice par sawal na aye, aisa kam hi hota hai. Kabhi active ko passive me badalna hota hai, kabhi passive ko pehchanna hota hai, aur kabhi jumla theek karna hota hai jahan is wrote jaisi ghalti chhupi hoti hai. Akhbar ki surkhiyan, sarkari notifications aur PPSC ki apni advertisements, teeno passive se bhari hui hain. Applications are invited. The last date has been announced. Ye jumle parhne ke liye bhi passive ki samajh lazmi hai. Aik wazeh baat pehle se sun lo. Ye lesson sirf buniyad hai. Is me hum sirf present aur past ke saada passive seekhen ge. Poora passive, har tense ke sath, modal ke sath aur hukum wale jumlo ke sath, Level 2 me alag lesson me ayega. Buniyad pakki ho to wo lesson asaan lagega."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Active aur passive ka farq pehle samajh lo"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Dekho, har jumle me aik kaam hota hai aur aik karne wala. Jab jumla karne wale se shuru ho to wo active hai. The teacher checked the papers. Yahan teacher aage hai, kaam peeche. Lekin kabhi kabhi karne wala aham nahi hota, kaam aur jis par kaam hua wo aham hota hai. Tab jumla ulta kar diya jata hai. The papers were checked. Ab papers aage hain, aur karne wala ya to peeche chala gaya ya ghayab ho gaya. Isi ulti surat ko passive voice kehte hain."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Urdu me bhi ye roz hota hai. Hum kehte hain ke darkhwastein talab ki gayi hain. Kis ne talab ki, ye nahi bataya. Khana pakaya gaya. Kis ne pakaya, ghayab. Urdu ki yehi gayi, gaya wali surat English me passive hai. Jab bhi Urdu me gaya ya gayi sunai de, samajh lo ke English me passive banega."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Passive banta kese hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Banane ka tareeqa teen kadmo me hai aur hamesha yehi teen kadam chalte hain. Pehla kadam, jis par kaam hua hai usay jumle ke aage le ao. Doosra kadam, us ke sath be ki munasib shakal lagao, is, are, was ya were. Teesra kadam, verb ki teesri shakal lagao. Bas, passive tayyar hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Misaal se dekho. Active hai: He writes a letter. Letter ko aage lao. Letter aik hai, is liye is lagega. Phir writes ki teesri shakal written. Jumla bana: A letter is written by him. Ab past ki misaal lo. Active hai: She wrote a letter. Letter aage aya. Waqt past hai, is liye was lagega. Phir written. Jumla bana: A letter was written by her. Dekha? Be ka faisla waqt aur aage wale noun se hota hai, aur aakhri shakal hamesha teesri hoti hai. Written kabhi wrote nahi banta, aur is ke sath wrote kabhi nahi ata."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Present aur past ka saada passive"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Is lesson me hum sirf do waqto par rahen ge. Present me is aur are ke sath teesri shakal ati hai. English is taught in our school. The rooms are cleaned daily. Past me was aur were ke sath teesri shakal ati hai. The fort was built in 1648. The windows were broken in the storm. Aik hai to is ya was, zyada hain to are ya were. Ye faisla aage wale noun se hota hai, purane karne wale se nahi. Yehi chhoti si baat aksar ghalti karwati hai, is liye isay zehen me bitha lo."),
      LessonBlock.heading("By wala hissa: kab aye, kab na aye"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Passive ke aakhir me aksar by ke sath karne wala ata hai. The poem was written by Iqbal. Yahan karne wala aham hai, is liye by ke sath aya. Lekin har jagah by lagana zaroori nahi. Agar karne wala maloom hi nahi, to by ghayab rahega. My bicycle was stolen. Kis ne churayi, maloom nahi, by a thief likhna fazool hoga. Agar karne wala aam sa hai, log ya koi bhi, tab bhi by hat jata hai. He was arrested last night. Police ka zikr karna zaroori nahi, sab ko pata hai ye kaam police hi karti hai. Qanoon ye hai: karne wala aham aur khaas ho to by se batao, warna jumla us ke baghair zyada saaf hota hai. Aur aik chhoti si khabardari, by ke baad me, him, her, us, them ate hain, I, he, she, we, they nahi. By him sahi hai, by he ghalat hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Passive kab behtar hota hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab ye samajh lo ke passive istemal hi kyun karte hain. Teen jagah par passive active se behtar hota hai. Pehli, jab karne wala maloom na ho. The bank was robbed at night. Doosri, jab kaam karne wale se zyada aham ho, jaise sarkari elan me. The date of the test has been fixed. Yahan kis ne fix ki, is se kisi ko gharz nahi, date aham hai. Teesri, jab karne wale ka naam lena munasib na ho ya baat narmi se kehni ho. Mistakes were made. Daftari zuban is liye passive se bhari hoti hai. Akhbar bhi yehi karta hai. Five people were injured in the accident."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Board par qanoon Angrezi me"),
      LessonBlock.rule("Board par passive ka qanoon kuch yun likha jata hai. In the passive voice, the object of the active sentence becomes the subject. The verb becomes be plus the third form: is written, are written, was written, were written. The doer, if mentioned, comes at the end with by: by him, by the teacher. The doer is dropped when it is unknown or unimportant. Aur aakhri aham line ye hai: the form of be depends on the new subject and the tense, and the main verb is always in the third form, never the second."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Misaalein board se"),
      LessonBlock.example("Urdu is spoken in Pakistan.", note: "Bolne wale aam log hain, zikr fazool hai. Is liye passive aya aur by ghayab hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("This school was built in 1950.", note: "Bananay wale maloom nahi aur aham bhi nahi. Past hai, is liye was built."),
      LessonBlock.example("The letter was written by her.", note: "Karne wali khaas hai, is liye by her aya. By she kehna ghalat hota."),
      LessonBlock.example("The thieves were arrested last night.", note: "Giraftari police ne ki, sab ko maloom hai. By police likhne ki zaroorat nahi."),
      LessonBlock.example("The test is held every year in June.", note: "Har saal hone wala mamla hai. Present passive hai, is held."),
      LessonBlock.example("My watch was stolen from the hostel.", note: "Chor maloom nahi. By lagana mumkin hi nahi."),
      LessonBlock.example("English is taught in almost every school.", note: "Present me is aur teesri shakal taught. Taught verb ki teesri shakal hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("The new bridge was opened by the chief minister.", note: "Yahan karne wala aham aur khaas hai, is liye by ke sath aya."),
      LessonBlock.example("All the tickets were sold in one day.", note: "Tickets zyada hain, is liye were aya. Be ka faisla aage wale noun se hua."),
      LessonBlock.example("The room is cleaned every morning.", note: "Roz ka mamla hai. Present passive, is cleaned."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Ye kahan kaam aata hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Sach ye hai ke sarkari aur akhbari angrezi passive ke baghair adhuri hai. PPSC ki advertisement kholo to likha hoga: Applications are invited from suitable candidates. The candidates will be informed by post. Asal imtehan me bhi notices, reports aur surkhiyan isi zuban me ati hain. Rozmarra me bhi hum kehte hain ke bijli band kar di gayi hai, result ka elan kar diya gaya hai. Urdu ke gaya, gayi wale jumle samajh lo to English passive parhna asaan ho jata hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab paper wale andaaz ke do jumle dekho."),
